  "description": "ZULGES crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H112 Gd6 O33. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.567-3.742 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.29-112.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd6(μ4-O)(OC2H4OMe)16]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
